wStatus":"generated","inputHash":"29aeda438f32fba4ecc50f40df28d111054716b0161e44151486701b541e9995","summary":"\"Migration has been happening, in varying forms, for millennia but it still elicits fear and mistrust, and not just on the part of the \"receiving\" society. Communities from where people migrate often disapprove of the migrants' decision and consider it treacherous. The recent reawakening of the debate about migration in the new millennium has evoked intense emotion particularly in the United States and Europe. Global Crossings cuts through the jungle of myth, falsehood and misrepresentation that dominates the debate, clarifying the causes and consequences of human migration. Why do millions of people continue to risk their lives, and oftentimes lose it, in the pursuit of a chance to establish themselves in a foreign land? The book first looks at the immigrant experience, which connects the present to the past, and America to the rest of the world, and explores who immigrants are and why they move. The conduct of today is no different than that in the past. And contrary to the claims by immigration critics, the patterns of contemporary migration do not differ fundamentally from those of other epochs. Global Crossings then discusses immigration and culture. To what degree are foreigners culturally different? Can natives adapt? Can immigrants assimilate into the new society?","publicationYear":2013,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Emigration and immigration","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Immigrants","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"SOCIAL SCIENCE","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Discrimination & Race Relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Minority Studies","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Emigration & Immigration","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Migration","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United states, emigration and immigration","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Immigrants, united states","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa"}],"displaySummary":"The recent reawakening of the debate about migration in the new millennium has evoked intense emotion particularly in the United States and Europe. Global Crossings cuts through the jungle of myth, falsehood and misrepresentation that dominates the debate, clarifying the causes and consequences of human migration. Why do millions of people continue to risk their lives, and oftentimes lose it, in the pursuit of a chance to establish themselves in a foreign land? The book first looks at the immigrant experience, which connects the present to the past, and America to the rest of the world, and explores who immigrants are and why they move. The conduct of today is no different than that in the past. And contrary to the claims by immigration critics, the patterns of contemporary migration do not differ fundamentally from those of other epochs. Global Crossings then discusses immigration and culture. To what degree are foreigners culturally different? Can natives adapt? Can immigrants assimilate into the new society?","primaryTopic":"Immigration, Refugees & Borderlands","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Race & Ethnicity","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Race & Ethnicity","mappedSubject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily addresses migration issues through the lens of race and ethnicity, while also discussing broader societal and political implications.","id":"subject-evidence-book-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Discrimination & Race Relations","mappedSubject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa","id":"subject-evidence-book-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa-6"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Emigration and immigration","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa","id":"subject-evidence-book-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-alvaro-vargas-llosa-4"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"SOCIAL SCIENCE","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-global-crossings-immigration-civilization-and-america-